# Cloudflare Web Analytics site token.
#
# LEAVE THIS UNSET IN PRODUCTION. Web Analytics is configured for automatic
# injection, so Cloudflare adds the beacon to the HTML at the edge and the
# page already reports without any help from the build. Setting this would
# add a second beacon and double-count every visit.
#
# It exists as a fallback: edge injection depends on Cloudflare being able to
# rewrite the response, so if it ever stops working, setting this variable in
# Workers Builds > Settings > Variables restores measurement without a code
# change. To check whether edge injection is working, request the live site
# with a browser User-Agent and grep for '"token":' -- Cloudflare does not
# rewrite HTML for a plain curl, so the naive check reports a false negative.
#
# The value is the "site tag" from the dashboard: Analytics & Logs >
# Web Analytics > Manage site > JS snippet, where it appears as
# data-cf-beacon='{"token": "..."}'. It is also the siteTag query parameter in
# the dashboard URL.
PUBLIC_CF_BEACON_TOKEN=
